IMPORT prelude

-- Medicines Act 1975 (Singapore) -- who needs which licence to deal in medicinal products and the exemptions from licensing
-- (ss 5 to 8), who may sell medicines by retail (ss 24, 26, 27, 29), what a medical advertisement may not claim (ss 49 to 51 and the
-- First Schedule), the due-diligence and warranty defences (ss 64, 65), and the maximum penalties and composition (ss 20, 35, 50,
-- 51, 53, 66, 72).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/MA1975.txt, with amendments
-- to Act 31 of 2022 (in force 1 November 2022) and S 759/2022 shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 12 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a trader, pharmacist,
-- practitioner or advertiser meets. Not encoded: the meaning of "medicinal product" (s 3), the licensing authority's procedure
-- and the factors it weighs (ss 10 to 19), export certificates (s 22), adulteration and purchaser protection beyond the defences
-- (ss 31 to 33), labelling and containers (ss 44 to 48, which are regulation-making powers), powers of entry, seizure and
-- forfeiture (ss 56 to 61), and s 77 (products moved to the Health Products Act 2007 by order). Nothing in any order or
-- regulation under the Act was read: which products are on the general sale list or are prescription-only is a fact supplied
-- by the user.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules conventions. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Medicines Act 1975 -- dealing, retail sale and advertising`

§§ `5 to 8 -- which licences a dealing needs`

-- s 5(1): "Except in accordance with a licence ... (called in this Act a product licence)" a person must not, in circumstances to
-- which the section applies, sell, supply or export, or procure the sale, supply, export, manufacture or assembly of, a medicinal
-- product. (3) for an imported product the section applies where the dealer "has himself or herself imported the product or
-- procured its import"; (4) for a product not imported, where the dealer "is responsible for the composition of the product".
-- (2): "A person must not import any medicinal product except in accordance with a product licence or an import licence."
-- s 6(2): manufacture or assembly needs a manufacturer's licence; (3) selling "by way of wholesale dealing" needs a wholesale
-- dealer's licence. s 2(2)(a): wholesale dealing is selling to a buyer who buys to resell or supply in a business, "except that
-- it does not include any such sale by the person who manufactured it". s 6(4): a manufacturer's licence does not authorise
-- making products for sale, supply or export unless the holder also holds the product licence or makes them "to the order of a
-- person who is the holder of such a product licence".
-- s 7(1), (2): ss 5 and 6 do not apply to what is done "in a hospital by or under the supervision of a pharmacist" in preparing,
-- dispensing or assembling (on a practitioner's prescription, or on the pharmacist's own judgment for a person present).
-- (3): nor to preparation, dispensing and assembly "by or under the supervision of a practitioner" for a patient or animal under
-- the practitioner's care. (4): those exemptions do not apply to veterinary biologics "except where such veterinary biologics
-- are prepared in a veterinary centre".
-- s 8(1): ss 5 and 6 do not apply to a herbal remedy made on premises the business occupies and can close to the public, sold
-- for a particular person at that person's request "and in that person's presence" on the seller's judgment as to treatment.
-- (2): nor to a herbal remedy whose plants are only dried, crushed or comminuted and which is sold "without any written
-- recommendation ... as to the use of the remedy".
DECLARE Dealing HAS
    `imports the product` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sells, supplies or exports the product` IS A BOOLEAN
    `imported it or procured its import` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is responsible for its composition` IS A BOOLEAN
    `manufactures or assembles the product` IS A BOOLEAN
    `makes it for sale, supply or export` IS A BOOLEAN
    `makes it to the order of a product licence holder` IS A BOOLEAN
    `sells to buyers who resell in their business` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is the manufacturer of what it sells` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is done in a hospital under a pharmacist` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is done by a practitioner for a patient or animal in care` IS A BOOLEAN
    `concerns veterinary biologics prepared outside a veterinary centre` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a herbal remedy made on closable premises for a person present` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a herbal remedy only dried, crushed or comminuted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `comes with a written recommendation as to use` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a product licence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds an import licence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a manufacturer's licence` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds a wholesale dealer's licence` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 7 exemption applies` IF
        (    `the dealing`'s `is done in a hospital under a pharmacist`
         OR  `the dealing`'s `is done by a practitioner for a patient or animal in care`)
    AND (NOT `the dealing`'s `concerns veterinary biologics prepared outside a veterinary centre`)

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 8 exemption applies` IF
        `the dealing`'s `is a herbal remedy made on closable premises for a person present`
    OR  (    `the dealing`'s `is a herbal remedy only dried, crushed or comminuted`
         AND (NOT `the dealing`'s `comes with a written recommendation as to use`))

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sections 5 and 6 do not apply` IF
    `the section 7 exemption applies` `the dealing` OR `the section 8 exemption applies` `the dealing`

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a product licence is needed` IF
        (NOT `sections 5 and 6 do not apply` `the dealing`)
    AND `the dealing`'s `sells, supplies or exports the product`
    AND (    `the dealing`'s `imported it or procured its import`
         OR  `the dealing`'s `is responsible for its composition`)

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the import is unlicensed` IF
        (NOT `sections 5 and 6 do not apply` `the dealing`)
    AND `the dealing`'s `imports the product`
    AND (NOT `the dealing`'s `holds a product licence`)
    AND (NOT `the dealing`'s `holds an import licence`)

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a wholesale dealer's licence is needed` IF
        (NOT `sections 5 and 6 do not apply` `the dealing`)
    AND `the dealing`'s `sells to buyers who resell in their business`
    AND (NOT `the dealing`'s `is the manufacturer of what it sells`)

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the manufacture is unlicensed` IF
        (NOT `sections 5 and 6 do not apply` `the dealing`)
    AND `the dealing`'s `manufactures or assembles the product`
    AND (    (NOT `the dealing`'s `holds a manufacturer's licence`)
         OR  (    `the dealing`'s `makes it for sale, supply or export`
              AND (NOT `the dealing`'s `holds a product licence`)
              AND (NOT `the dealing`'s `makes it to the order of a product licence holder`)))

-- s 20(1): "any person who contravenes any of the provisions of sections 5 and 6 ... shall be guilty of an offence".
GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealing contravenes sections 5 and 6` IF
        (    `a product licence is needed` `the dealing`
         AND (NOT `the dealing`'s `holds a product licence`))
    OR  `the import is unlicensed` `the dealing`
    OR  `the manufacture is unlicensed` `the dealing`
    OR  (    `a wholesale dealer's licence is needed` `the dealing`
         AND (NOT `the dealing`'s `holds a wholesale dealer's licence`))

§§ `24, 26, 27 -- retail sale only by or under a pharmacist`

-- s 24: "a person must not sell by retail or supply in circumstances corresponding to retail sale any medicinal product which is
-- not a medicinal product on a general sale list, unless that person is or acts under the personal supervision of a pharmacist".
-- s 25: a general sale list product may be sold by anyone, subject to prescribed conditions.
-- s 27(1): s 24 does not apply to supply "(a) by a doctor or dentist to his or her patient; or (b) by a hospital" for
-- administration on a doctor's or dentist's directions; (2) by a veterinary surgeon for an animal under his or her care; (3) to a
-- herbal remedy sold at premises the business occupies and can close to the public, where the plants are subjected to "drying,
-- crushing or comminuting, with or without diluting with water, but not any other process".
-- s 26: a medicinal product "must not be sold by means of an automatic machine unless it is a medicinal product in the automatic
-- machine section of a general sale list".
DECLARE RetailSale HAS
    `the product is on the general sale list` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the seller is or acts under the personal supervision of a pharmacist` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a doctor or dentist supplies a patient` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a hospital supplies on a doctor's or dentist's directions` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a veterinary surgeon supplies for an animal in care` IS A BOOLEAN
    `it is a simple herbal remedy sold at closable premises` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the sale` IS A RetailSale
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sale contravenes section 24` IF
        (NOT `the sale`'s `the product is on the general sale list`)
    AND (NOT `the sale`'s `the seller is or acts under the personal supervision of a pharmacist`)
    AND (NOT `the sale`'s `a doctor or dentist supplies a patient`)
    AND (NOT `the sale`'s `a hospital supplies on a doctor's or dentist's directions`)
    AND (NOT `the sale`'s `a veterinary surgeon supplies for an animal in care`)
    AND (NOT `the sale`'s `it is a simple herbal remedy sold at closable premises`)

GIVEN `in the automatic machine section` IS A BOOLEAN, `meets the prescribed conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it may be sold from a vending machine` IF
    `in the automatic machine section` AND `meets the prescribed conditions`

§§ `29 -- prescription-only medicines`

-- s 29(2): for a product specified by order, "(a) a person must not sell by retail, or supply in circumstances corresponding to
-- retail sale, ... except in accordance with a prescription given by an appropriate practitioner"; "(b) a person must not
-- administer (otherwise than to himself or herself) any such medicinal product unless the person is an appropriate practitioner
-- or a person acting in accordance with the directions of an appropriate practitioner". (1): the order names which of doctors,
-- dentists and veterinary surgeons are appropriate practitioners. Exemptions by order (s 29(3)) are not encoded.
GIVEN `has a prescription from an appropriate practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the retail sale of a prescription-only product is lawful` IF
    `has a prescription from an appropriate practitioner`

GIVEN `to oneself` IS A BOOLEAN, `is an appropriate practitioner` IS A BOOLEAN, `acts on an appropriate practitioner's directions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may administer a prescription-only product` IF
    `to oneself` OR `is an appropriate practitioner` OR `acts on an appropriate practitioner's directions`

§§ `49 to 51 and First Schedule -- medical advertisements`

-- s 49(2): "advertisement" does not include spoken words except in a sound recording, a film soundtrack, or a broadcast. (3):
-- neither the sale of a product in a labelled container or package nor a leaflet supplied with a product "relating solely to
-- medicinal products of that description" is the issue of an advertisement. (4): a "medical advertisement" relates or appears to
-- relate to a medicinal product or a device used or represented to be used for a medicinal purpose.
-- s 51(1): a person must not publish "(a) any medical advertisement which directly or indirectly claims, indicates or suggests
-- that the article advertised will prevent, alleviate or cure any disease or condition specified in the First Schedule; or (b) any
-- advertisement referring to any skill or service relating to the treatment of any disease or condition affecting the human
-- body". (2): not an advertisement distributed only to, or in a publication for circulation mainly among, practitioners,
-- pharmacists, nurses and midwives, or those training to be any of them.
-- First Schedule: 1 Blindness, 2 Cancer, 3 Cataract, 4 Drug addiction, 5 Deafness, 6 Diabetes, 7 Epilepsy or fits,
-- 8 Hypertension, 9 Insanity, 10 Kidney diseases, 11 Leprosy, 12 Menstrual disorders, 13 Paralysis, 14 Tuberculosis,
-- 15 Sexual function, 16 Infertility, 17 Impotency, 18 Frigidity, 19 Conception and pregnancy.
DECLARE Condition IS ONE OF
    `blindness`
    `cancer`
    `cataract`
    `drug addiction`
    `deafness`
    `diabetes`
    `epilepsy or fits`
    `hypertension`
    `insanity`
    `kidney diseases`
    `leprosy`
    `menstrual disorders`
    `paralysis`
    `tuberculosis`
    `sexual function`
    `infertility`
    `impotency`
    `frigidity`
    `conception and pregnancy`
    `the common cold`
    `asthma`
    `heart disease`
    `obesity`
    `insomnia`

GIVEN `the condition` IS A Condition
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the condition is in the First Schedule` IF
    CONSIDER `the condition`
    WHEN `the common cold` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `asthma` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `heart disease` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `obesity` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `insomnia` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

DECLARE Advert HAS
    `is live spoken words` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is only the product's labelled container or package` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a leaflet supplied with the product about that product only` IS A BOOLEAN
    `relates to a medicinal product or medical device` IS A BOOLEAN
    `claims to prevent, alleviate or cure` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the condition claimed` IS A Condition
    `refers to a skill or service for treating a human condition` IS A BOOLEAN
    `goes only to practitioners, pharmacists, nurses, midwives or trainees` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the advert` IS AN Advert
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is an advertisement` IF
        (NOT `the advert`'s `is live spoken words`)
    AND (NOT `the advert`'s `is only the product's labelled container or package`)
    AND (NOT `the advert`'s `is a leaflet supplied with the product about that product only`)

GIVEN `the advert` IS AN Advert
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `publishing it contravenes section 51` IF
        `it is an advertisement` `the advert`
    AND (NOT `the advert`'s `goes only to practitioners, pharmacists, nurses, midwives or trainees`)
    AND (    (    `the advert`'s `relates to a medicinal product or medical device`
              AND `the advert`'s `claims to prevent, alleviate or cure`
              AND `the condition is in the First Schedule` (`the advert`'s `the condition claimed`))
         OR  `the advert`'s `refers to a skill or service for treating a human condition`)

-- s 50(1): issuing a false or misleading advertisement relating to medicinal products is an offence. (5)(a): "it is a defence for
-- the person to prove ... that the person did not know, and could not with reasonable diligence have discovered, that the
-- advertisement or representation was false or misleading".
GIVEN `issued a false or misleading advertisement` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved could not with reasonable diligence have discovered it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `guilty under section 50(1)` IF
    `issued a false or misleading advertisement` AND (NOT `proved could not with reasonable diligence have discovered it`)

§§ `64, 65 -- due diligence and warranty defences`

-- s 64(3): the act-or-default-of-another provision, with its due-diligence defence in (2), "applies to sections 31 to 33, 44 to
-- 47 and 50 to 52". s 65(2): the warranty defence "applies to section 31(b), sections 32, 33 and 44 to 47".
-- s 65(1): the accused must prove (a) purchase in Singapore with a written warranty that the article could lawfully be sold,
-- (b) no reason at the time to believe otherwise, (c) the article was in the same state as when purchased. (3): only if the
-- accused has, "not later than 7 clear days before the date of the hearing", sent the prosecution a copy of the warranty and a
-- notice, and a like notice to the warrantor. (6): a name or description in an invoice "is deemed to be a written warranty".
DECLARE Provision IS ONE OF
    `section 24 (retail sale without a pharmacist)`
    `section 29 (prescription-only)`
    `section 31(a) (adulterating)`
    `section 31(b) (selling an adulterated product)`
    `section 32 (not of the nature or quality demanded)`
    `section 33 (pharmacopoeia standards)`
    `section 44 (labelling)`
    `section 50 (false or misleading advertisement)`
    `section 51 (prohibited medical advertisement)`

GIVEN `the provision` IS A Provision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 64 applies` IF
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `section 24 (retail sale without a pharmacist)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `section 29 (prescription-only)` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the provision` IS A Provision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `section 65 applies` IF
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `section 31(b) (selling an adulterated product)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 32 (not of the nature or quality demanded)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 33 (pharmacopoeia standards)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `section 44 (labelling)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE Warranty HAS
    `bought in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `with a written warranty or a descriptive invoice` IS A BOOLEAN
    `no reason to believe otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
    `in the same state as when bought` IS A BOOLEAN
    `clear days' notice before the hearing` IS A NUMBER
    `warrantor also notified` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the provision` IS A Provision, `the warranty` IS A Warranty
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the warranty defence succeeds` IF
        `section 65 applies` `the provision`
    AND `the warranty`'s `bought in Singapore`
    AND `the warranty`'s `with a written warranty or a descriptive invoice`
    AND `the warranty`'s `no reason to believe otherwise`
    AND `the warranty`'s `in the same state as when bought`
    AND `the warranty`'s `clear days' notice before the hearing` AT LEAST 7
    AND `the warranty`'s `warrantor also notified`

§§ `20, 35, 50, 51, 53, 66, 72 -- maximum penalties and composition`

-- s 20(6): offences under s 20(1), (2), (3) -- "a fine not exceeding $5,000 or ... imprisonment for a term not exceeding 2 years
-- or ... both"; (7) s 20(5) (failing to comply with a s 19(2) notice) -- "a fine not exceeding $2,000". s 35(3): offences under
-- s 35(1), (2) (including contravening ss 24, 26, 29) -- $5,000 or 2 years; (4) breaching s 25 conditions -- $2,000. s 50(7) and
-- s 51(3): $5,000 or 2 years. s 53(2): failing to furnish copies of advertisements -- $2,000. s 66(3): false warranty -- $5,000 or
-- 2 years. s 72: the licensing authority may compound any offence "by accepting ... a sum not exceeding $2,000".
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `dealing without a licence`
    `false statement in a licence application`
    `ignoring an information notice`
    `selling a pharmacy-only product without a pharmacist`
    `breaching general sale list conditions`
    `false or misleading advertisement`
    `prohibited medical advertisement`
    `not furnishing copies of advertisements`
    `giving a false warranty`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum fine` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `ignoring an information notice` THEN 2000
    WHEN `breaching general sale list conditions` THEN 2000
    WHEN `not furnishing copies of advertisements` THEN 2000
    OTHERWISE 5000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the maximum imprisonment in years` IS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `ignoring an information notice` THEN 0
    WHEN `breaching general sale list conditions` THEN 0
    WHEN `not furnishing copies of advertisements` THEN 0
    OTHERWISE 2

GIVEN `the sum offered` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the sum may be accepted in composition` IF
    `the sum offered` AT MOST 2000
